<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zeng Guofan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zeng Guofan was a Chinese scholar-official and military leader who raised and commanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-army">Xiang Army</a>, which played a central role in suppressing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiping-rebellion">Taiping Rebellion</a>. He was also a leading figure in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/self-strengthening-movement">Self-Strengthening Movement</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> profile notes that the success of such <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-chinese">Han Chinese</a> regional armies transferred real military power away from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> court.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zeng-guofan.jpg" alt="Zeng Guofan" width="297" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tseng_Kwo-Fan.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
